# Skills that are referenced by name but deliberately not written yet.
#
# validate.py downgrades a reference to one of these from an error to a warning.
# That keeps the roadmap visible instead of letting a broken chain read as clean.
#
# Rule: a slug belongs here only if some SKILL.md already points at it. Delete the
# line the moment the skill is written — validate.py flags stale entries (PLN001).

# React meta-frameworks other than Next.js. mir-frontend Gate 5 offers these as
# alternatives; only the Next.js module exists so far.

# Angular reactivity tier. mir-frontend Gate 0 lists it as a selectable tier.

# Cloud provider modules. mir-cloud is provider-neutral by design and hands off to
# a provider module at Gate 5 for service mechanics. The pillar and its decision
# tables ship first; the per-provider modules follow.
